---
import Layout from '../../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { localPath } from '../../../lib/urls';
import { softwareProjects } from '../../../data/software-projects';
const project = softwareProjects.find(p => p.id === 'pilketos')!;
---
<Layout title="Pilketos — Software Case Study" description="Architecture and engineering overview of Pilketos, a school election application using React, Vite, and Supabase.">
  <article class="section case-study">
    <div class="container">
      <nav class="breadcrumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href={localPath('/portfolio/')}>Portfolio</a> <span aria-hidden="true">/</span> <span>Pilketos</span></nav>
      <p class="eyebrow">Case Study · Web Application</p>
      <h1>Pilketos</h1>
      <p class="intro">A web application exploring how election administration, polling-station operations, and result reporting can be organized for a student-council election.</p>
      <div class="case-availability" role="note"><span class="availability-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Source available · Interactive demo unavailable</span></div>
      <figure class="case-diagram">
        <div class="diagram-header"><span>APPLICATION FLOW</span><span>CONCEPTUAL · NOT A SCREENSHOT</span></div>
        <ol>
          {project.workflow.map((step, i) => (
            <li>
              <span class="flow-number">{String(i + 1).padStart(2, '0')}</span>
              <strong>{step}</strong>
              {i < project.workflow.length - 1 && <span class="flow-arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</span>}
            </li>
          ))}
        </ol>
        <figcaption>High-level information architecture reconstructed from repository modules. No user data is depicted.</figcaption>
      </figure>
      <div class="project-facts">
        <div><span>Current phase</span><strong>Development / demonstration</strong></div>
        <div><span>Frontend</span><strong>React + Vite</strong></div>
        <div><span>Backend</span><strong>Supabase Auth + PostgreSQL</strong></div>
        <div><span>Repository</span><strong><a href={project.repository} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Open on GitHub ↗</a></strong></div>
      </div>
      <section class="case-section">
        <h2>The problem</h2>
        <p>Student elections involve more than displaying candidates. Administrators also need to manage voters, polling-station assignments, operational staff, the election flow, and results. These concerns benefit from a consistent system rather than disconnected spreadsheets.</p>
      </section>
      <section class="case-section">
        <h2>Application structure</h2>
        <p>The source repository contains separate routes and views for election setup, candidates, voters, staff, polling stations (TPS), voting, dashboard, and results. Authentication is implemented using Supabase with an application-level user role profile.</p>
        <div class="feature-grid">
          <div class="feature"><strong>Election setup</strong><p>Manage the organizational structure of the election.</p></div>
          <div class="feature"><strong>TPS workflow</strong><p>Separate polling-station and staff interfaces.</p></div>
          <div class="feature"><strong>Voter administration</strong><p>Dedicated voter and participant management views.</p></div>
          <div class="feature"><strong>Results</strong><p>Dedicated results view and monitoring dashboard.</p></div>
        </div>
      </section>
      <section class="case-section evidence-section">
        <h2>What the source demonstrates</h2>
        <div class="evidence-grid">
          <div><h3>Inspectable implementation</h3><p>Distinct React routes cover election setup, candidate records, voters, TPS and staff interfaces, and result pages. The Supabase client and authentication context are present in the repository.</p></div>
          <div><h3>Not yet verified</h3><p>A fully operating public vote, security against duplicate voting, election-scale load handling, and end-to-end production readiness have not been demonstrated here.</p></div>
        </div>
      </section>
      <section class="case-section">
        <h2>Deployment and responsible demonstration</h2>
        <p>This project's source is hosted on GitHub and includes GitHub Pages deployment automation. Its Supabase project was inactive when this case study was prepared, so a functional live voting demo is <strong>not claimed</strong>. A future public demo should run on synthetic voters and a separate database from any real election.</p>
      </section>
      <section class="case-section">
        <h2>Technology</h2>
        <div class="tags">{project.technologies.map(tech => <span class="badge">{tech}</span>)}</div>
        <p>Future improvements will be documented with reproducible evidence instead of claims about security, throughput, or reliability that have not been tested.</p>
      </section>
      <a href={localPath('/portfolio/')} class="back-link">← All software projects</a>
    </div>
  </article>
</Layout>
<style>
  .case-study .container { max-width: 900px; }
  .case-availability { display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:.55rem;border:1px solid var(--border-color);background:var(--bg-secondary);border-radius:999px;padding:.5rem .9rem;margin:.4rem 0 2rem;font-size:.82rem;font-weight:650;color:var(--text-secondary); }
  .availability-dot { width:.53rem;height:.53rem;border-radius:50%;background:var(--accent-color); }
  .case-diagram { margin:0 0 2.8rem;padding:clamp(1.1rem,3vw,2rem);border-radius:20px;background:var(--bg-secondary);border:1px solid var(--border-color); }
  .diagram-header { display:flex;gap:.7rem;justify-content:space-between;flex-wrap:wrap;color:var(--accent-color);font-size:.68rem;font-weight:750;letter-spacing:.11em; }
  .diagram-header span:last-child { color:var(--text-muted); }
  .case-diagram ol { display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,minmax(0,1fr));list-style:none;gap:.75rem;margin:1.5rem 0 1rem; }
  .case-diagram li { position:relative;display:flex;flex-direction:column;min-height:96px;gap:.8rem;border:1px solid var(--border-color);border-radius:12px;padding:1rem;background:var(--bg-primary);font-size:.9rem; }
  .flow-number { color:var(--accent-color);font-size:.75rem;font-weight:800; }
  .flow-arrow { position:absolute;right:-14px;top:50%;transform:translateY(-50%);color:var(--accent-color);z-index:1;font-size:1.3rem;font-weight:800; }
  .case-diagram figcaption { font-size:.78rem;color:var(--text-muted); }
  .evidence-grid { display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr));gap:1rem; }
  .evidence-grid > div { border:1px solid var(--border-color);border-radius:13px;padding:1.3rem;background:var(--bg-secondary); }
  .evidence-grid h3 { font-family:var(--font-sans);font-size:.99rem; }
  .evidence-grid p {font-size:.89rem;margin:0;}
  .breadcrumb { font-size:.9rem; color:var(--text-muted); margin-bottom:2.2rem; }
  .eyebrow { text-transform:uppercase; font-size:.78rem; letter-spacing:.11em; font-weight:700; color:var(--accent-color); }
  h1 { font-size:clamp(3rem,8vw,4.6rem); }
  .intro { font-size:1.23rem; max-width:730px; }
  .project-facts { display:grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(2,1fr); border:1px solid var(--border-color); border-radius:var(--border-radius); margin:2.7rem 0 3.2rem; overflow:hidden; }
  .project-facts > div { padding:1.2rem; border-bottom:1px solid var(--border-color); }
  .project-facts span { display:block; font-size:.8rem; color:var(--text-muted); }
  .project-facts strong { display:block; font-size:.98rem; margin-top:.2rem; }
  .case-section { margin:2.8rem 0; }
  .case-section h2 { padding-bottom:.7rem; border-bottom:1px solid var(--border-color); }
  .feature-grid { display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr)); gap:1rem; }
  .feature { background:var(--bg-secondary); padding:1.2rem; border:1px solid var(--border-color); border-radius:var(--border-radius); }
  .feature p { font-size:.91rem; margin-top:.4rem; margin-bottom:0; }
  .tags { display:flex; gap:.5rem; flex-wrap:wrap; }
  .tags .badge { border:1px solid var(--border-color); background:var(--accent-light); }
  .back-link { display:inline-flex; margin-top:1rem; }
  @media(max-width:640px) { .project-facts,.feature-grid,.evidence-grid,.case-diagram ol {grid-template-columns:1fr;} .flow-arrow { right:auto;left:50%;top:auto;bottom:-20px;transform:translateX(-50%) rotate(90deg); } }
</style>
